_backoff_failure)\\(\\) \\{.*?^\\}\"` ALSO extracts prune_docker_caches, so after relocation the harness gets two definitions of it.","tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py:44-45 comment: 'the two helper functions under test, which are defined further down' — the below-single-flight layout assumption the relocation invalidates.","tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py:116,118 assert exactly one `docker image prune` and `src.count('prune_docker_caches') >= 3`."],"finding":"The Scope's inventory for the relocated `prune_docker_caches()` symbol omits an existing structural consumer: tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py drives prune_docker_caches and record_backoff_failure by regex-extracting their function blocks AND by splitting the script on the '# ── single-flight' marker for its prefix. The plan lists only the three runtime call sites and claims the callers are 'otherwise unchanged', but relocating prune_docker_caches to ~150 (above the single-flight boundary at line 189) places it inside BOTH the wholesale-sourced `prefix` and the separately-extracted `funcs`, double-defining it in the harness, and violates the harness's stated 'defined further down' assumption. This test file appears in neither the Scope nor the Testing sections.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fef91576f62653cc9","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope — 'relocate the existing prune_docker_caches() definition from line ~245 up into the helper block (~150) … its body and its two existing call sites are otherwise unchanged'","norm_id":"n8b821fe89aa7cac4","priority":0.165,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py: after prune_docker_caches moves above the '# ── single-flight' marker, `_run_helpers` includes the function in both `prefix` and `funcs`, injecting a duplicate definition into the bash harness — the plan's implementer will not know to update this test because it is absent from the inventory.","tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py::test_no_uncapped_or_stray_prunes_in_script: its `src.count('prune_docker_caches') >= 3` and single-image-prune invariants are directly coupled to the relocation and new call site, yet the test is unlisted, so a regression here is undetected until CI."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"prune_docker_caches() is defined at autodeploy.sh:245, AFTER the line-228 no-op exit where the plan calls reclaim_under_pressure (which invokes prune_docker_caches). Bash resolves function names at call time, so invoking prune_docker_caches at line 228 with its definition still at 245 would hit an undefined function; the plan places the new helpers at ~150 but does not require moving prune_docker_caches above the line-228 call site.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f156753e6dc9a51ce","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 3 / Scope (autodeploy.sh:228 call site vs prune_docker_caches at autodeploy.sh:24